•	 FRS 102 provides an accounting policy choice to expense or capitalise development
expenditure. FRS 102.18.8H sets out that an entity may recognise an intangible asset arising
from development if it can demonstrate the following criteria:

– For sale and leaseback transactions, FRS 102.20.77(d), requires disclosure of: the
reasons for these transactions and the prevalence; the key terms and conditions;
payments not included in the lease liability; the cash flow effect in the reporting period;
and as applicable, the accounting policy choice to apply paragraph 20.123(a)(ii) when
the transfer is a sale
